+ // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ // Cross-area composition facades (A5 x A2 x A6)
+ //
+ // `docs/runtime-design/area-composition-spec.md` assigns A5 three composition
+ // duties that no single area module owns on its own:
+ //
+ //   - Pair 3 (A5 + A2): the A5 budget plan is injected before the wave
+ //     scheduler starts; a started wave is immutable, so a plan can only change
+ //     the *next* wave (`appliesToWave`).
+ //   - Pair 5 (A5 + A6): after a resume, A5 re-runs `ContextBudgetPlanner`.
+ //     A budget read back from the checkpoint is stale and must never be reused.
+ //   - Stage 3 criterion 3.6: pause -> resume -> planner re-executes, not stale.
+ //
+ // This module is the composition facade for those duties. It is deliberately
+ // thin and read-only towards the production ladder:
+ //   - `ContextBudgetPlanner` only READS `compression-planner.ts` thresholds via
+ //     `resolveTierThresholds` (earlier-only clamp, production defaults as the
+ //     backstop). It never replaces the five-tier ladder, never mutates
+ //     `CompressionArtifact`, and never blocks a turn on estimation failure.
+ //   - Wave changes always go through `ResourceAwareWaveScheduler.rePlan`, which
+ //     already rejects started/completed waves (criterion 3.9).
+ //   - A5 budget breaches are read from the existing deprecation registry
+ //     (`degrade_to_default_budget`), not re-implemented here.
+ //
+ // See: docs/runtime-design/area-composition-spec.md (Pair 3 / Pair 5)
+ // See: docs/runtime-design/development-manual.md (criterion 3.6, A5 module CAN/MUST NOT)
